# Chapter 11, part 4: messages of other programs, odd wordings and the
# messages of the Error Log.  The exit status of the programs and the
# messages of their command lines are in the last part of the chapter, which
# the release edition leaves out.
.h2 Messages of the programs that Strata runs [msg-other]
.ix Messages, other programs
.ix Third party messages
Strata runs LaTeX, the print command, the spell checker and a few programs that
install fonts.  Their messages are passed on inside the messages above or are
named by them; this section says what the commonest ones mean for a Strata
user.  The words are those of the other programs and can change with their
versions; this chapter does not list them all.
.h3 LaTeX [msg-other-latex]
.ix LaTeX, error messages
.ix First error line
.ix Undefined control sequence
LaTeX stops at an error and Strata shows the first error line of its log (it
begins with an exclamation mark and a space) and the line after it, in
{c:LaTeX failed: } on the screen or after the name of the document on the
error output.  A mistake in an equation or a picture does not stop a print:
the Printer prints the piece in its long form ({n:eq-print-fail}).  What stops
it is mostly a missing package or file.
.table 31 29
Text | Meaning and what to do
{c:! I can't find file `NAME'.} | A file that the document needs is missing: a
 | picture file, or a file of the font.  Check the name and where it is.
! LaTeX Error: File `NAME.sty' not found. | A LaTeX package is not installed.
 | A font of TeX Font Association needs it: install it ({n:msg-other-font}),
 | or choose another font. {x:print-prereq} lists the packages of the
 | prerequisites.
! Package NAME Error: TEXT | A package of LaTeX refused something.  The text
 | says what.
! TeX capacity exceeded, sorry [TEXT] | The document is too large for the
 | settings of LaTeX; print it in parts (a range of sections).
! Undefined control sequence. | A command that LaTeX does not have.  In a
 | document of Strata this comes from a hand-made text of a marker or an
 | unusual font package.
.end
.h3 The print command [msg-other-lp]
.ix lp, messages
.ix CUPS, messages
The text after {c:lp failed (status N): } is the text of lp.
.table 31 29
Text | Meaning
lp: Error - The printer or class does not exist. | The queue named in Printer
 | is not known to the print system.  The Print panel's {k:F2} list shows the
 | queues that exist.
request id is NAME (1 file(s)) | The job was taken. NAME is the number to give
 | to the print system to cancel it.  Shown in
 | {c:Wrote ... and sent it to QUEUE (...)}.
.end
.h3 The installation of fonts [msg-other-font]
.ix Font installation, messages
.ix Install failed
.ix CTAN
The command Install Now of TeX Font Association downloads an archive and
enables its map file, with the programs kpsewhich, curl, unzip, mktexlsr and
updmap-user.  While it runs a box titled Installing font names the step:
"Downloading NAME..." with the size received so far, "Unpacking NAME...",
"Making the file list of TeX (mktexlsr)..." and "Enabling the map file MAP
(updmap-user)...".  {k:Esc} stops the download only.  The results are shown in a
box titled Install failed or Installed.
.table 33 27
Message | Meaning and what to do
Cannot make a temporary directory | The directory for the download cannot be
 | made.  Check the room where the download is made.
Font N has a character that cannot be used (only letters, digits and . _ - + =
 , are allowed) | The list of fonts is refused before it is written
 | ({n:appcfg}); the field has another character.
Installation cancelled | {k:Esc} stopped the download.  Nothing is installed and
 | the partial file is removed.
Installed in DIR | The archive is unpacked into DIR and the font is installed.
kpsewhich did not run (is TeX installed?) | TeX is not installed, or the
 | program that finds its directories is missing.
The archive could not be downloaded from URL | curl failed: no network, the
 | name of the archive is wrong, or the server is not reachable.
The archive could not be unpacked | The program unzip failed or is missing.
The name of the archive or of the map file has a character that cannot be used
 | The fields CTAN Archive to Download or Map File to Enable have a bad
 | character or a slash.
This font has no archive to download | The field CTAN Archive to Download is
 | empty.
updmap-user failed to enable the map file | The font is unpacked but its map
 | file was not enabled.  Run the program by hand or fix the name.
.end
.h2 Messages that read oddly [msg-faults]
.ix Odd wordings
.ix Marker, title of refusal box
.ix Messages, wording
A few messages say less than they should or are headed with a title that does
not fit.  They are listed so that a user is not misled.
.table 29 31
Message | Explanation
Any panel refusal of the File, Print, Preview, Macros or Library commands | The box has the title of the panel; read the text.
cannot open file, read error, write error | These words of the document reader
 | name neither the file nor the system's reason.  The name was typed in the
 | panel just before.
The PDF cannot replace the document | Only the Print panel checks this.
.end
.h2 Messages of the Error Log [msg-errlog]
.ix Error Log, messages
.ix Print Error, messages
.ix Find Next Error, messages
.ix Faults of a document, messages
A document that cannot be printed as it is gets its faults named: in the Error
Log pages of the PDF, in Print Error markers in the text, and in lines on the
error output.  The faults have one text each, listed here with their kind: an
error is a piece that cannot be set and is printed as text, a warning is a
piece that is set with something lost.  Each fault has a short name, which is
given in square brackets in the lines of the error output.
.h3 The faults [msg-errlog-faults]
.ix Faults, list
.table 35 9 16
Message | Kind | Name
{c:A counter has reached 4294967295 and stays there; its later uses show the same number.}
 | Warning | counter-limit
{c:A Keep was started while another is still open; the first has no End Keep.}
 | Error | keep-doubled
{c:A page break or column break inside a table or a line with tabs cannot be
 honored; it is printed as text.} | Warning | marker-incell
{c:Invalid Include request: A part with sections must be in the last block of
 its section.} | Error | include-place
{c:Invalid Include request: The file "NAME" cannot be found.}
 | Error | include-missing
{c:Invalid Include request: The file "NAME" cannot be read.}
 | Error | include-unreadable
{c:Invalid Include request: The file "NAME" includes itself, directly or
 through other parts.} | Error | include-loop
{c:Invalid Include request: The file "NAME" is not a Strata document or is
 damaged.} | Error | include-damaged
{c:Invalid Include request: The Include marker cannot be in a headline.}
 | Error | include-place
{c:Invalid Include request: The Include marker has no file name.}
 | Error | include-noname
{c:Invalid Include request: The Include marker must be alone in its block.}
 | Error | include-place
{c:Invalid Include request: The parts are nested more than 8 levels deep.}
 | Error | include-deep
{c:LaTeX markers are not allowed in this print: the text of this one is not
 written and the marker is printed as text.} | Warning | latex-marker-off
{c:NAME markers are not typeset by Strata; the marker is printed as text.}
 | Warning | marker-unsupported
{c:No font has the character U+XXXX; it is printed as [U+XXXX].} | Warning
 | | char-missing
{c:Picture file not found: NAME (looked in PLACES).} | Error
 | | picture-missing
{c:TeX rejects the equation (WHY), so it is printed as text.} | Error
 | | equation-refused
{c:TeX stopped without saying why, so no picture is printed.} | Error
 | | picture-refused
{c:Text that depends on an If cuts across the sections: a section whose
 parent is left out moves up a level.} | Warning | if-structure
{c:The cross-reference points at a section that is not in the document (or not
 in this part of it).} | Warning | xref-unresolved
{c:The equation cannot be read: it is too long or damaged, so it is printed as
 text.} | Error | equation-unreadable
{c:The equation is empty.} | Warning | equation-empty
{c:The equation is not valid TeX math, so it is printed as text.} | Error
 | | equation-invalid
{c:The operator of this If is missing or not known: the operators are = # < >
 <= >=, and # means not equal.} | Error | if-bad-operator
{c:The picture cannot be used (WHY), so it is printed as text.} | Error
 | | picture-refused
{c:The picture file cannot be given to TeX here.} | Error | picture-link
{c:The picture file NAME cannot be read: REASON.} | Error | picture-unreadable
{c:The picture file NAME is incomplete or damaged.} | Error | picture-damaged
{c:The picture file NAME is of a type that cannot be printed (only PNG, JPEG,
 PDF and PostScript can).} | Error | picture-type
{c:The picture marker has no file name.} | Error | picture-noname
{c:The special symbol is not known to Strata; it is printed as text.}
 | Warning | symbol-unknown
{c:The text of this LaTeX marker is too long or damaged, so it is not written
 and the marker is printed as text.} | Error | latex-marker-unreadable
{c:The value of the counter cannot be worked out; it is printed as text.}
 | Warning | counter-unresolved
{c:The value of this If is not allowed: REASON} | Error | if-bad-literal
{c:These Ifs are nested too deep: the limit is ten.} | Error | if-too-deep
{c:This Else has no If before it.} | Error | else-unmatched
{c:This End Keep has no Start Keep before it.} | Error | keep-unmatched
{c:This Endif has no If before it.} | Error | endif-unmatched
{c:This If already has an Else.} | Error | else-doubled
{c:This If does not begin with the name of a variable: a name starts with a
 letter.} | Error | if-no-variable
{c:This If has no Endif after it.} | Error | if-unclosed
{c:This If has no expression: it needs a variable, an operator and a value,
 such as COLOR = red.} | Error | if-empty
{c:This If has nothing after the operator to compare the variable with.}
 | Error | if-no-literal
{c:This Start Keep has no End Keep after it.} | Error | keep-unclosed
.end
NAME is a marker name or a file name, WHY the reason that the checks gave,
REASON the reason of the system.  An error of the log of LaTeX is also a
fault: its text is the first error line of TeX ({n:msg-other-latex}).  What to
do: correct the thing that the text names (a missing picture file, an equation
that is not TeX math, a Keep without its End Keep, a part that an Include
marker cannot find) and print again; {x:eq-
print-fail} says what the Printer prints in place of an equation that fails.
.h3 The place of a fault [msg-errlog-place]
.ix Fault, place
.table 36 24
Place | Meaning
{c:Section TAG TITLE, block N, column N, line N, NAME marker} | The place in
 | words: the section by its number and title, then the block, the column and
 | the line, and the marker that is wrong.  The parts that do not apply are
 | left out.
{c:Title page, block N} | The fault is on the title page.
{c:Block N} | The document is not structured.
{c:Item N} | A place that is not in a block.
{c:line N of the file that TeX read} | An error of TeX that could not be put
 | in a block.
{c:no position} | The place is not known.
.end
.h3 On the message line [msg-errlog-line]
.ix Print Error, message line
.ix Ctrl-F8
.table 29 31
Message | After
{c:N print errors removed} | Remove Print Errors took out all of them.
{c:No print errors} | Find Next Error, Find Previous Error and Remove Print
 | Errors: there are no Print Error markers in the document.
{c:No print errors.} | The end of the line of a good print when there was
 | none.
{c:Print error N of M: TEXT} | Find Next Error went to the marker N of M; TEXT
 | is the fault. {c:Wrapped to the start.} or {c:Wrapped to the end.} stands
 | before it when the search went round.
{c:Print Error (read only; Del removes it)} | The title of the box that shows
 | the text of a marker ({k:Alt-F12} on it).
{c:Print Error removed} | Remove Error took out the marker under the cursor.
{c:PRINT FAILED: Preview shown in spite of errors of LaTeX: TEXT} | A Preview
 | whose pages LaTeX made in spite of an error of its own.
{c:Print: no print errors} | After a Print that found none.
{c:Print: PRINT FAILED, N print errors (Ctrl-F8 finds the next)} | After a
 | Print that found errors: the number of markers made.
 | {c:Preview done: PRINT FAILED, N print errors (Ctrl-F8 finds the next)} after a Preview.  With
 | warnings only the words {c:PRINT FAILED, } are not there.
{c:The cursor is not on a Print Error} | Remove Error with the cursor
 | elsewhere.
.end
{x:print-errmarks} and {x:print-errline} describe the markers and the keys.
